% ADJ36 — ED chest-pain ACS risk rulebook
%
% Rulebook in ADJ14 grammar. Every contribute() / prior() clause
% carries a citation (after %, ProbLog-style line comment) so the
% audit trail can resolve every LR back to a published source.
%
% This file is the source the framework lowers into LP19e
% PriorClause / ContributionClause / JointContributionClause
% structures per ADJ11 v2. The executable proof is in
% adj36-execute.py.

% --- Prior --------------------------------------------------------

prior(0.10, acs).
% Source: Pope JH et al., "Missed Diagnoses of Acute Cardiac Ischemia
% in the Emergency Department." NEJM 1995;342(16):1163-70.
% ED chest-pain ACS prevalence in the undifferentiated population.

% --- Demographic risk-factor contributors -------------------------

contributes(1.5, pmh(hypertension), acs).
% Source: HEART Score; Six AJ et al., "Chest pain in the emergency
% room: value of the HEART score." Neth Heart J 2008;16(6):191-6.
% LR derived from HEART score discriminant statistics. [empirical]

contributes(1.8, pmh(smoker), acs).
% Source: HEART Score; Six et al. 2008. [empirical]

% --- Symptom-quality contributors ---------------------------------

contributes(2.5, symptom_quality(pressure_like), acs).
% Source: Panju AA et al., "The rational clinical examination: Is
% this patient having a myocardial infarction?" JAMA 1998;280(14):
% 1256-63. Pooled LR for "pressure" descriptor (range 1.5-3.0).

contributes(2.0, associated_symptom(diaphoresis), acs).
% Source: Panju et al. JAMA 1998. Pooled LR for diaphoresis present
% (range 1.7-2.7).

% --- Precipitator (the unobserved atom in this case) --------------

contributes(2.5, precipitator(exertional), acs).
% Source: Diamond GA, Forrester JS. "Analysis of probability as an
% aid in the clinical diagnosis of coronary-artery disease."
% NEJM 1979;300(24):1350-8. Exertional onset is one of the three
% pillars of typical angina (range 2.0-4.0).

contributes(0.6, precipitator(rest), acs).
% Source: Same series. Rest pain can be ACS (unstable angina) but
% the LR is mildly protective in undifferentiated ED population
% because rest pain has many non-cardiac causes.

contributes(0.8, precipitator(positional), acs).
% Source: [empirical] Slight protective LR — positional pain is
% often MSK or pleuritic in origin.

% --- Negative contributors (protective evidence) ------------------

contributes(0.5, vital_signs(within_normal_limits), acs).
% Source: Panju et al. JAMA 1998. Normal vital signs in chest pain
% reduce ACS likelihood by approximately half.

contributes(0.4, denied(ecg_acute_st_changes), acs).
% Source: Pope et al. NEJM 1995. ECG without acute ST changes
% lowers but does not exclude ACS — residual NSTEMI/UA rate
% means LR ≈ 0.4 rather than ≈ 0.1.

% --- Interaction terms (synergy beyond product-of-individual-LRs) -

contributes_jointly(1.3,
                    [symptom_quality(pressure_like),
                     associated_symptom(diaphoresis)],
                    acs).
% Source: [empirical] Clinical experience — the combination of
% pressure-like chest pain WITH diaphoresis is more diagnostic of
% ACS than the product of individual LRs would suggest.

% --- Query --------------------------------------------------------

query(acs).

% --- End of rulebook ----------------------------------------------
